<title>UK: UK's Clarke raises car tax with inflation.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke raises car tax with inflation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor Kenneth Clarke said on Tuesday he would increase car excise duty by five stg per year, or around the rate of inflation.</p>
<p>He said the cost of a lorry tax disc would be frozen for the seventh year.</p>
<p>In addition, vehicle excise duty would be reduced by up to 500 stg for lorries meeting very stringent emission standards.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 2274</p>
</text>
